<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Money is mostly lost to drift rather than to disasters: the subscription
    that renewed at a price nobody agreed to, the quiet increase, the
    category that's been forty pounds a week more than you'd have guessed
    for two years.
  </p>
  <p>
    None of that is visible without a ledger, and every convenient way to get
    one asks for your bank login.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">No bank connection, on purpose</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    Handing your banking credentials to software — or to the aggregator
    behind it — is a bad trade, and it turns out not to be necessary. Your
    bank already offers a statement export. Import that, or log things by
    hand as they happen, and the ledger fills up without anybody holding
    keys to your account.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    The honest cost is that somebody has to do the import. That's a real
    chore, and it's the price of the rest of this page.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What it does with it</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Learns your sorting, once") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Put a merchant in a category and you've taught a rule. Next month it
        sorts itself. Every rule you've taught is visible and editable — the
        app is never quietly deciding things you can't inspect.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Reads the month back to you") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        In plain language, with the specific cuts worth making rather than a
        pie chart and an implication. It knows what you meant to spend,
        because you told it.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Finds the subscriptions") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Including the free trial from three years ago. Cancelling one is a
        tool of its own, because the decision was never the hard part — the
        retention phone call was.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Stays yours") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Your complete transaction history is among the most revealing things
        about you. It sits on your disk, and nothing is sold, scored, or
        shown to anyone.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">No scores, no streaks</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    There's no rating of you, no notification calling a coffee a mistake,
    and no gamified points for frugality. The ledger's job is to make the
    picture visible. What you do about it is yours.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-5">
    <%= link_to "How the budget uses this →", about_feature_path("budget"), class: "text-primary-700 hover:underline" %>
  </p>
</section>
